# IspeakLLM for Python (WSGI, Django, Flask)

Serves your IspeakLLM bundle (`ispeakllm generate` writes `.ispeakllm/bundle.json`) from any WSGI app with the same HTTP behaviour as the JS adapters: `llms.txt`, `llms-full.txt`, page Markdown (`/x.md` and `Accept: text/markdown`), conditional `304`, the AI Conformance Manifest, policy files and per-path policy headers. HTML responses only gain `Vary: Accept`, `Link` and policy headers.

Python standard library only (3.8+); Django and Flask are only needed for their own glue. Licence: MIT.

Written new for the OSS release: the GoPlainly versions had no Django/Flask source.

## Install

```sh
pip install ispeakllm-wsgi        # or copy ispeakllm_wsgi/ into your project
```

## Any WSGI app

```python
from ispeakllm_wsgi import IspeakLLMMiddleware
application = IspeakLLMMiddleware(application, bundle_path=".ispeakllm/bundle.json")
```

Options: `bundle_path` or `bundle` (an already-parsed dict), `cache_control` (default `public, max-age=300`).

## Flask

```python
from ispeakllm_wsgi.flask import init_app
app.config["ISPEAKLLM_BUNDLE"] = ".ispeakllm/bundle.json"   # default
init_app(app)
```

## Django

```python
# settings.py
MIDDLEWARE = ["ispeakllm_wsgi.django.IspeakLLMMiddleware", *MIDDLEWARE]
ISPEAKLLM_BUNDLE = BASE_DIR / ".ispeakllm" / "bundle.json"       # default ".ispeakllm/bundle.json"
ISPEAKLLM_CACHE_CONTROL = "public, max-age=300"                  # optional
```

Put it first so `/x.md` is answered before `CommonMiddleware` (APPEND_SLASH) and URL routing. Wrapping `application` in `wsgi.py` with the WSGI middleware works too.

## Test

```sh
python3 -m unittest discover -s integrations/python/tests
```

Boots `wsgiref` on a free 127.0.0.1 port with `IspeakLLMMiddleware` in front of the reference host and runs `conformance/adapter-http/runner.mjs --level core`. The Django and Flask glue is not exercised (neither is installed here); both are thin wrappers over the tested core.
